      "A sound survey in the fictional city of Merrow began with an apparent contradiction. Two streets produced similar average sound levels, but residents described one as restful and the other as exhausting. The research team did not assume that either the instruments or the residents must be wrong. An average compresses a changing sequence into one number, whereas a listener experiences particular events in particular circumstances. A short burst of sound outside a bedroom at night may matter more than a longer, predictable sound during the working day. The team designed a second survey to investigate these differences.",
